  { number := 215, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 216, text := "" },
  { number := 217, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 218, text := "" },
  { number := 219, text := "1. A grant that keeps copyright is treated as still leaving a copyright holder, and remaining copyright is treated as still letting a later contract take the work (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 220, text := "2. The most important Surmount work in this repository is dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense; companion Lean treats an Unlicense dedication as having no remaining copyright in the model (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 221, text := "3. Ideas are treated as not scarce; two people can hold the same idea at once; generosity of ideas is the default this repository chooses (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 222, text := "4. Numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree are released under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license; the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT; essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 223, text := "5. Refusing a tool the author cannot improve is treated as RSI process residual and is not treated as a claim that every product is Unlicense (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 224, text := "6. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true; proofs live in separate Lean modules; a mash that hides the split is treated as `False`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 225, text := "7. Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URL; a numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags also contains the host `proofofkeags.com`; theorems cover exactly what they state (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 226, text := "8. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 227, text := "9. fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; number 0009 is this specification and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 228, text := "10. The named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 229, text := "" },
  { number := 230, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming Surmount product. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
