  { number := 238, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 239, text := "" },
  { number := 240, text := "1. fargo is not specified. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, or 0011 for fargo. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 241, text := "2. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 242, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is this specification. Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 243, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 244, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then withdrawn, and is now Unlicense by operator order. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 245, text := "" },
  { number := 246, text := "### 6.2 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 247, text := "" },
  { number := 248, text := "1. This document specifies the Unlicense for this specifications repository. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 249, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds. The match is not claimed done. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 250, text := "3. `lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean` proves those claims. `lean/Surmount.lean` composes stack identities including this specification as number 0009. `0009_Unlicense.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0009.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that Slake emit already matches `ELF`. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use. They are not a proof that every file in a clone is Unlicense." },
