  { number := 270, text := "5. Surmount Systems is specified in `0010_Surmount_Systems.md`. Surmount Systems is not this specification." },
  { number := 271, text := "6. Companion models for CATE (`lean/CateSpec.lean` encodings, `lean/CateProofs.lean` theorems), RSI (`lean/RsiSpec.lean`, `lean/RsiProofs.lean`), Continuous Integration (`lean/CiSpec.lean`, `lean/CiProofs.lean`), beastdb (encodings and proofs under `lean/` for that product), SSSSS (`lean/SssssSpec.lean`, `lean/SssssProofs.lean`), Systems Lean (`lean/SystemsLeanSpec.lean`, `lean/SystemsLeanProofs.lean`), Formal Vibefication (`lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean`, `lean/FormalVibeficationProofs.lean`), Unlicense (`lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean`, `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean`), Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`lean/TechTreeSpec.lean`, `lean/TechTreeProofs.lean`), Majestic Memex (`lean/MemexSpec.lean`, `lean/MemexProofs.lean`), Lean Machine (`lean/LeanMachineSpec.lean`, `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`), and the CATE word catalog (`lean/VocabularySpec.lean`, `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`) place encodings in Spec modules and theorems in Proofs modules. Collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` are encodings with proofs in `lean/VocabularyCollisionProofs.lean`. Mixing those in one mash is `False` under `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Sibling line encodings remain a separate split." },
