  { number := 280, text := "" },
  { number := 281, text := "First publication of Unlicense as numbered specification 0009 with file name `0009_Unlicense.md`. The operator assigned 0009 to fill the gap after Vocabulary was folded into CATE. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then withdrawn; it is now Unlicense by operator order. A numbered Vocabulary file remains forbidden. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Records that a grant that keeps copyright still lets a later contract take the work. Requires the most important Surmount work in this repository (numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree) to be dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense so it stays the common heritage of anyone who seeks it, outside a later private claim. Records that ideas are not scarce and that two people can hold the same idea at once. Requires authors to release numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license. Records that the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT and that essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense. Records that refusing a tool the author cannot improve is RSI process residual and is not a claim that every product is Unlicense. Records Formal Vibefication as the split that encodes this specification in Lean and keeps proofs in separate modules, with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Treats a mash of spec encodings and their proofs that hides the split as nonconforming. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use." },
